'''Haicang International Airport''' ({{lang|ca|Aeroport Internacional de Haicang}}; [[IATA airport code|IATA]]: HAI, [[ICAO airport code|ICAO]]: HAIB) is an international airport serving [[Haicang]], a city in the [[La Marina]] comarca of [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. The airport is located on the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] coast and serves a community with historical ties to the [[Fosian Balboan people|Fosian Balboan]] population. The city's name derives from the Zong-era {{w|Hokkien}} term 海港 (''haikáng'', "sea port"), reflecting its origin as a Zong naval base and ship repair facility during the [[Zong Balboa]] period.

The airport handles both domestic and international traffic. [[Aeroístmus]] operates services from both [[Sant Cristòfor International Airport|Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Cecilio Ríos International Airport|Sant Bart]], and [[Sinchew Air]] operates international services to [[Tamsui]].

